# Definition of done

A work package is complete only when applicable items from technical guide §36 pass.

## Required for behavior changes

- Happy path plus empty/loading/error/timeout/cancel/reconnect/retry states
- Auth and object-level authorization tests
- Role-privacy tests where session payloads are involved (two-browser Playwright when applicable)
- Analytics/product events without sensitive properties
- Migrations understood; types regenerated
- Provider calls bounded; no new overlapping dependencies without justification

## Commands (when app exists)

`pnpm check`, `pnpm test`, relevant `pnpm test:e2e` / `pnpm test:db`

Use `playwright-cli` for browser E2E work.

## Reject these changes

- Second `User`/`Session`/`Exam` model instead of the domain model
- Privileged Supabase queries in client components
- Fetch full blueprint and hide examiner fields with CSS
- Provider presence as session-completion truth
- Unawaited serverless promise as the only background job mechanism
- Hardcoded model names across feature files
- Full prompts/transcripts in error logs
- Editing a production migration in place
- “Done” without failure-state and authorization tests
- Large unrelated refactors or TODO placeholders without owner
- Polished UI while required product events are missing
